rule: EXPECTED_VALUE_CHANGED
note: the honest half of the same coin — the production fix genuinely
note2: changes the symbol the test calls, so the expectation update keeps
note3: its repair evidence and stays at warn. Normalisation must not
note4: over-reach into real behaviour changes.
origin: audit 2026-08-19, added with the fingerprint normalisation
=== before: billing.py ===
def invoice_total(items, tax):
    # BUG: ignores tax
    total = sum(items)
    return round(total, 2)
=== after: billing.py ===
def invoice_total(items, tax):
    total = sum(items) * (1 + tax)
    return round(total, 2)
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total():
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) == 100.0
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total():
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) == 105.0
